{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 15, :comments ["<b>Is it a small matter that you have taken my husband</b> — the meaning is: Is it a small matter from you, that you take for yourself my husband, as though you are his wife and I the maidservant — that you should further make yourself the mistress to take the mandrakes, in whose fragrance I delight? And it is possible that she desired them for Jacob's honor, to perfume his couch with them, for it is the way of women to do so, as it is written (Proverbs 7:17), \"I have sprinkled my bed with myrrh, aloes, and cinnamon\"; and therefore Leah said, \"Is it a small matter that you have taken my husband from me, that you should also take my son's mandrakes to entice him with them?\" And some say that the mandrakes are herbs that increase desire in women, derived from the language of \"the time of dodim\" (Ezekiel 16:8); and therefore Leah said, \"Is it a small matter that you have taken my husband,\" as I have mentioned."], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T04:21:46.250126231Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}